{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence","id":1310979,"title":"Other \"planes of existence\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-05-09T08:00:58-07:00","id":1310979,"title":"Other \"planes of existence\"","content":"In World of Darkness, Umbra has extremely rich structure: lots of different &quot;worlds&quot; with somewhat intricate relations between them. I always loved this particular aspect of the setting (which was itself inherited from Shadowrun and then repeated in Chronicles of Darkness). Taking into account the history of Exalted as a setting, I presume that something similar should be the case here. <br /> <br /> is it the case though? I jumped in to Exalted only with the current edition and I the core book you don't see much about complex structure of different words. For sure we have:<br /> - Underworld;<br /> - Malfeas;<br /> - Elsewhere (is it stil a placein Third Edition?, core book says it's &quot;metaphorical&quot;);<br /> - Yu-Shan (kind of);<br /> - Wyld (kind of);<br /> - Besides that, the description of sorcerous workings kind of implies that more &quot;micro worlds&quot; can be created. <br /> <br /> Clearly, this is not very little, but when compared to sheer abundance of different &quot;parts&quot; of Umbra in Mage: the Ascension, this picture seems kind of underwhelming, especially taking into account how wonderfully over-the-top this setting tends to be. However, I understand that possibly there could be much more described in the material from previous editions.<br /> <br /> So, what other &quot;worlds&quot; are there in the setting of Exalted. In general, should I rather think that &quot;Umbra&quot; carries over to Exalted and there will be a rich structure of worlds with their own strange internal laws that simply happened not to be described in the main book?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T08:06:30-07:00","id":1310981,"title":"","content":"Zen Mu. The underworld, while only touched on in the core, has vast kingdoms where time flows strange and things are weird. Malfeas is also getting sold a bit short here, with its forest of mirrors, river of quicksilver holding another city, and regions defined by grammar. You also have demenses where things go strange. Generally, however, exalteds other worlds are concretely other worlds\u2014there\u2019s a part of the underworld that reflects a specific part of creation but it\u2019s not overlapping exactly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T08:10:03-07:00","id":1310983,"title":"","content":"You forgot Autochthonia and maybe Zen Mu depending on how you count that one, nd there is a lot going on in these places that the Ex3 core does not really do a deep dive in. Or even mention in the case of Autobot. As well as the overall richness of Creation itself which has plenty of strangeness baked in with elemental demesnes and bizarre sorcerous ruins and all.<br /> <br /> You can turn to old 1e and 2e sources on a lot of these places to see some of that nuance and weirdness you were talking about but with the caveat some of it may be heavily being redone this edition by the time we get a good look at them. I know the Underworld at least is supposed to be getting heavily redone I think. I personally am a huge fan of the Compass Autochthonia book and attendant Alchemical lore in theirs and I know people who will die to defend Graceful Wicked Masques.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T08:58:05-07:00","id":1310995,"title":"","content":"High-Essence Infernals in 2.5 who have pursued the Devil Tiger path can carve their own pocket dimensions from their souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25282-heart-attacks","name":"Heart Attacks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25282_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T09:19:41-07:00","id":1310999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence#post1310979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In World of Darkness, Umbra has extremely rich structure: lots of different &quot;worlds&quot; with somewhat intricate relations between them. I always loved this particular aspect of the setting (which was itself inherited from Shadowrun and then repeated in Chronicles of Darkness). Taking into account the history of Exalted as a setting, I presume that something similar should be the case here.<br /> <br /> is it the case though? I jumped in to Exalted only with the current edition and I the core book you don't see much about complex structure of different words. For sure we have:<br /> - Underworld;<br /> - Malfeas;<br /> - Elsewhere (is it stil a placein Third Edition?, core book says it's &quot;metaphorical&quot;);<br /> - Yu-Shan (kind of);<br /> - Wyld (kind of);<br /> - Besides that, the description of sorcerous workings kind of implies that more &quot;micro worlds&quot; can be created.<br /> <br /> Clearly, this is not very little, but when compared to sheer abundance of different &quot;parts&quot; of Umbra in Mage: the Ascension, this picture seems kind of underwhelming, especially taking into account how wonderfully over-the-top this setting tends to be. However, I understand that possibly there could be much more described in the material from previous editions.<br /> <br /> So, what other &quot;worlds&quot; are there in the setting of Exalted. In general, should I rather think that &quot;Umbra&quot; carries over to Exalted and there will be a rich structure of worlds with their own strange internal laws that simply happened not to be described in the main book?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Other than Zen-Mu (which might not be a real &quot;place&quot; in a sense of the word of another world and is likely never going to be detailed since it's also kind of R'lyeh) and Autochthonia (which is still kind of like Creation in that it's a phyiscal realm with people and spirits in it, just different a lot in what the realm made of), there really sin't. Creation in general has not really been big on having the off-Creation stuff be super numerous. The Underworld in 3e is a lot like Wraith's Temepst in 3e, with the different realms fo the dead and the seas and Labyrnth connecting htem. Malfeas is enormous and made of the bodies of titans. The Wyld is kinda-infinite and has whatever is needed there. Elsehwere is kind of not really a &quot;place&quot; just &quot;Not here&quot;. Many spirits also ahve sanctums, but these are more pocket-dimensions extending from Creation, rather than a whole different realm.<br /> <br /> There's nothing, though, like the Umbra in Exalted. This is in part since Exalted is very focused on Creation and human endeavours therein. Having a universe of stuff beyond Creation kind of dilutes what makes Creation itself interesting and the main place to do things for the majority of the setting's residents. Gods live more or less either in Heaven or in the world itself (with sanctums kind of being an extension fo that).<br /> <br /> This isn't necessarily bad, as a note. I think that just because other settings have big complex cosmologies beyond the main world, means that that is <i>a priori</i> what a setting should be. The Umbra doens't add a lot ot Creation since the spirits of the world exist in Creation wiht people. Quantity doesn't equal quality and all that, especailly with realms of existance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T10:07:11-07:00","id":1311008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1310999#post1310999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This isn't necessarily bad, as a note. I think that just because other settings have big complex cosmologies beyond the main world, means that that is <i>a priori</i> what a setting should be. The Umbra doens't add a lot ot Creation since the spirits of the world exist in Creation wiht people. Quantity doesn't equal quality and all that, especailly with realms of existance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this is mainly a matter of aesthetics. I genuinly love going completely weird. It seemed to me that Exalted has enough intrinsic weirdeness within the setting. However, I can imagine many themes that could stretch that weirdness a bit too far if placed in the Creation itself. Especially when it comes to heavily redefining rules of local metaphysics. It seemed to me that Exalted might have enough place for all kinds of quirky stuff. However, as I understand, Maelfas and Zen Mu are supposed to have a lot of such venues.<br /> <br /> A follow up question: is Elsewhere a place? Corebook of 2nd edition seems to imply that. Moreover, Autochtonia seems to be described as literally being separated from the creation by Elsewhere. 3rd edition core book seems to imply that it's just a metaphor. <br /> <br /> Another question: how should I depict Wyld? I kind of imagined it as pure chaos with no interesting things gonig on &quot;there&quot;. Should I for example imagine Fair Folk as literally coming<i> from</i> Wyld, or just, sort of, materializing in Creation. I would vastly prefer the former, but it seemed to me that it is heavily non-canonical.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T10:22:58-07:00","id":1311010,"title":"","content":"Elsewhere was a place in 2e. In 3e it is just a place that is Not Here and not deeply defined. I think at your table it could easily be a place if you want but the books so far have not in 3e been keen to draw a hard rule there","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T11:30:18-07:00","id":1311019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence#post1310979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clearly, this is not very little, but when compared to sheer abundance of different &quot;parts&quot; of Umbra in Mage: the Ascension, this picture seems kind of underwhelming, especially taking into account how wonderfully over-the-top this setting tends to be.</div> </div> </div> </div> Worth noting that, unlike the old World of Darkness, Creation doesn't need to pass as the real world. It's a fantasy setting, and it has room for a lot of strangeness the WoD would have to consign the Umbra.<br /> <br /> Just for example, there are cities and palaces of cloudstuff high above the earth, and if you can find a way up there you can discuss esoterica with the cloud people; there are spirits and monsters all through the wilderness; there are islands that a really just oceanic behemoths, or giant jellyfish, or whatever you need. Go into the deep woods, and you might fight a nexus of power where the inhabitants are half rose, or a city of snakemen, or an ancient, oracular tree.<br /> <br /> Creation, on its own, can be plenty otherworldly, if that's what you need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T11:56:08-07:00","id":1311026,"title":"","content":"Exalted, unlike Mage the Ascension, has no Gauntlet. The Weaver has yet to break the world, dividing spirit from flesh. As such, it\u2019s really only in Creation where spirits can even become immaterial, with most other realms treating spirit stuff as equally material as normal stuff.<br /> <br /> This does not mean there is a shortage of other realms, however.<br /> <br /> As you and others have noted, the \u201cmain\u201d other realms are Malfeas, the Underworld, Yu-Shan, and the Wyld. As other people have noted, Elsewhere isn\u2019t really a place in any sense of the word. In addition to those, gods can create their own Sanctums, small pocket realms where the god dwells. Sorcerous Workings, Artifacts, and some Exalted charms can create similar spaces.<br /> <br /> However, it\u2019s also important to note that each of those Realms can be broken up into lots of different areas. The most \u201cnormal\u201d of these other realms, Yu-Shan, is \u201cMagitech New York/Tokyo, enlarged to the size of a continent.\u201d Even if you need to maintain a certain degree of consistency over the physics of the place, it is going to be hella spectacular.<br /> <br /> It seems like the Underworld is going to be fairly different in 3e, but it sounds like it\u2019ll be interesting.<br /> <br /> Malfeas is hard to get to, but every Yozi is effectively an entire planet/universe unto itself, with variant physical laws as appropriate. Malfeas himself is a multi-dimensional hyper-Dysonsphere type structure orbiting a Green Sun with all the attendant weirdness that implies. Oramus, the Dragon Beyond the World, a Primordial of irrationality who could only be bound by his own wings, is attached to the Beyond which is apparently an even weirder place than the Pure Wyld.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, the Wyld is where reality breaks down and Physical Laws are enforced by someone\u2019s will. Raksha and other dangerous entities live here. There are places you can go, like Zen-Mu or the castles of various Raksha, but it\u2019s somewhat difficult to know what changes will be made in 3e and whether we\u2019ll get details on, say, the Scorpion Empire or not.<br /> <br /> You might want to consider looking into the book Games of Divinity from 1e, as that has some cool info about Malfeas.<br /> <br /> Also, Creation can get pretty weird. Once The Realm drops, you might want to read it\u2019s section on The Caul, because it has a city that bursts into flames every night and another one which only exists in memory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T12:48:29-07:00","id":1311037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1311008#post1311008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, this is mainly a matter of aesthetics. I genuinly love going completely weird. It seemed to me that Exalted has enough intrinsic weirdeness within the setting. However, I can imagine many themes that could stretch that weirdness a bit too far if placed in the Creation itself. Especially when it comes to heavily redefining rules of local metaphysics. It seemed to me that Exalted might have enough place for all kinds of quirky stuff. However, as I understand, Maelfas and Zen Mu are supposed to have a lot of such venues.<br /> <br /> A follow up question: is Elsewhere a place? Corebook of 2nd edition seems to imply that. Moreover, Autochtonia seems to be described as literally being separated from the creation by Elsewhere. 3rd edition core book seems to imply that it's just a metaphor.<br /> <br /> Another question: how should I depict Wyld? I kind of imagined it as pure chaos with no interesting things gonig on &quot;there&quot;. Should I for example imagine Fair Folk as literally coming<i> from</i> Wyld, or just, sort of, materializing in Creation. I would vastly prefer the former, but it seemed to me that it is heavily non-canonical.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Wyld gets divided into three sections: Bordermarches, which are the ones nearest to Creation but that have strange occurrences and &quot;bugs&quot; in reality, like a dark abandoned castle whose inhabitants get slowly turned to blood-craving beasts, or a flower field where you can taste the flowers' scent and hear their colors. Then there's Middlemarches, where the boundary between Creation and chaos gets blurry and physics seem to give way to strangeness (say, an ocean of words that still behaves like an ocean, but everything that enters it becomes literate and more ornate as if described by a very purple-prose-y author, and drowning in it is more akin to being maddened by knowledge and unceasing whispers until you dissolve into them). And then there's the Deep Wyld, where things get really crazy and it's the farthest you can go into chaos so expect... CHAOS. You'll have to figure out an example for that one~ There are also Wyld Pockets inside Creation, like little bubbles of chaos in an otherwise clean tapestry, so you can have Fair Folk and other Wyldspawn show up in Creation using those. The FF come from the Wyld, some could spawn in it, some could be birthed, some could come into being through some sort of ritual. Who knows! Go crazy!<br /> <br /> Also, there's a Raksha Noble in Adversaries of the Righteous called Adeimantus, I heavily recommend checking him out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T13:14:23-07:00","id":1311042,"title":"","content":"Yeah while the Wyld is Chaos, it's not like chaos where you cant reach an understanding, its chaos where concepts and things change frequently or at least that's how I tend to portray the Deep Wyld. A Realm where the boundaries of things and ideas becomes undefined and constantly changing from theme and design to another. A road of skittering gold would suddenly become a great serpent made from smoke which then Coils up to form a tower of crystalized anger. It's a place where you can never trust what you see and is all danger","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T15:25:08-07:00","id":1311071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1311010#post1311010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elsewhere was a place in 2e. In 3e it is just a place that is Not Here and not deeply defined. I think at your table it could easily be a place if you want but the books so far have not in 3e been keen to draw a hard rule there</div> </div> </div> </div>I've kind of looked at Elsewhere in 3E being a spatial equivalent of Schrodinger's Cat. It is everywhere and nowhere, a quantum state of unsure being. When an Exalt banishes their artifacts Elsewhere, they are using Essence to not observe the artifact so hard it enters this uncertain state. Like Schrodinger's Cat being both alive and dead because we cannot observe it to tell the truth of the matter, the Daiklaive is both here and not. <br /> <br /> Also, I remember seeing somewhere the devs say they didn't want Elsewhere to be a &quot;place&quot; this edition, but don't quote me on that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13696-knurlurzhad","name":"Knurlurzhad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13696_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T15:44:07-07:00","id":1311080,"title":"","content":"Before we get an official version, I'd look to the way a spirit sanctum is portrayed in the chapter fiction in Fangs at the Gate to create the correct <i>feel</i> without being constrained by the literal dimensions. You shift a bit and pass through the correct door, and you get a version of the physical that is polished and made fantastical. Don't frame it as a box.<br /> <br /> These things are dotted all over the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T16:34:33-07:00","id":1311090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1311042#post1311042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah while the Wyld is Chaos, it's not like chaos where you cant reach an understanding, its chaos where concepts and things change frequently or at least that's how I tend to portray the Deep Wyld. A Realm where the boundaries of things and ideas becomes undefined and constantly changing from theme and design to another. A road of skittering gold would suddenly become a great serpent made from smoke which then Coils up to form a tower of crystalized anger. It's a place where you can never trust what you see and is all danger</div> </div> </div> </div>Random interesting bit noted by the devs is Pure Chaos is probably not about anymore. But that jus tmostly means that there's usually somthing like, actually comprehendable to a human-like sapient being about. Even if it is still chaotic and dangerous and mutating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T16:38:37-07:00","id":1311095,"title":"","content":"Another thing to point out is that due to the nature of the Wyld, it's very possible to have strange, alien vistas being their own sort of world, such as with the Scorpion Empire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T21:31:14-07:00","id":1311142,"title":"","content":"Thinking on it, something like the Book of Worlds for Mage the Ascension probably would be useful for creating some strange places in Exalted. The descriptions of Horizon Reallms and the dimensions where each of the Spheres are paramount could provide inspiration for many things in Exalted, including demesnes.<br /> <br /> Actually, it is worth noting that Creation has Demesnes where tears turn to silver or water and air intermix freely, intelligent Manses that are bigger on the inside, Wyld Zones and Shadowlands that partake of the nature of other Realms, sites of ancient battles where anyone who dares set foot will be turned to crystal, and places that are just plane weird like that city built inside a demon\u2019s corpse or the one built in the Lap of a statue the size of a mountain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T23:18:38-07:00","id":1311167,"title":"","content":"What everybody is saying.<br /> <br /> In occult mistery/horror games, but otherwise set in our modern world, it becomes useful to have another worlds, so you can have weird magical adventures you couldn\u00b4t have in Earth, with weird races and monsters and strange climates and all the things that are more common in a fantasy world, but if you put them on Earth, you would break the setting, in the sense that &quot;Eh... If there are dragons, and floating crystal palaces, how the hell is the masquerade still going, and the world even slightly similar to our own?&quot;. So, these more... visual things are relegated to other worlds. The Umbra/Supernal Realms/Arcadia/The Dreaming of World of Darkness/Chronicle of Darkness, the Kelipahs of Silent Legions, the Otherzones of Unknown Armies (although with that game focus on humanity, they have been largely ignored. Third Edition is the first, I think, in which I have seen focus on an Otherzone that wasn\u00b4t a Room of Renunciation).<br /> <br /> In a strange, big, fantastical world like Creation? Some other worlds are useful (Malfeas, Yu-shan, the Underworld, mostly so kinds of spirits can live there, and you can go there nd have spirit adventures!), but I have had in my games shadowlands along a road where you entered into the Deads\u00b4 Realm by sleeping in the abandoned inn while travelling South, I have had adventures on Malfeas, uncontrolled demesnes which corrupted the waters and made plants grow in weird forms and transformed the animals who ate them, a forest clearing with a magical eternal tree under which, anything buried, would never rot and eternally preserve (and a player buried there the woman his character loved, because she was a crazy sorcerer obssessed with bringing her back to life. The player knew that was impossible, but wanted to play the story of someone becoming obssessed with an impossible thing and pacting with Deathlords and weird things from the Underworld. He left the game for college, but was an awesome player), a walking castle who &quot;lives&quot; in the middle of a ruined city but sometimes wander across and steals walls and cattle and kidnaps people, and nobody really knows why, a tower that was exactly the same overground and underground, being the underground part a Underworld reflection which could lead you to the Sea of Shadows, but you could only leave the Tower if someone outside opened the door for you (it wasn\u00b4t even a very special door, but you had to be invited to the Realm of the Living), underwater cities in which tribes of sharkmen fend off giant zombie fishes, or the underground Goblin Markets of Chiaroscuro. Oh, and a castle in which a Faewith the shapeof a beast used his servants, which took the shape of living objects and uncommon animals (for the region: they were parrots and monkeys in the North) to kidnap youngs from the village, both men and women, turn them into their brides, their special ones, and finally kill them when they finally disappoint him (not a fault of them: it was rigged from the start), to start the cycle a new! And a player is playing a sorcerer and want to summon demon-spiders to produce magical silks, and train refugees and create magical manufacturing villages in the middle of nowhere, Soviet planned cities style, to produce awesome clothes and ropes and sails with strong, magical, beautiful silk (so he can be rich as hell, yes, but also as a way to provide a new life to these refugees)<br /> <br /> And I favour a relatively &quot;normal&quot; version of Creation, in which there aren\u00b4t sorcerers in each corner and I\u00b4m more inspired by real societies and cultures than by pulp fantasy (although I\u00b4m a lawyer, I\u00b4m also an amateur historian. Love my damn history!). The Creations used by other groups will probably be stranger than mine.<br /> <br /> So, I don\u00b4t really see the need of Other Worlds so you can have real exploration. There is enough weird things in Creation!<br /> <br /> (Although I have never been a fan of the Umbra. I like to focus my games in a region or city, and in the groups and characters living there and the consequences of their actions, and I find that when the players spend half the time exploring far-off realms to no real connections to the place they are playing in... It dilutes the style I like to play, and my players are also not fans of roaming, travelling characters. So... When I put pocket realms, they are localized things, with influence in the place they are playing in. In my current &quot;Occult investigators in a Japanese High School&quot; game there is a pocket realm, they haven\u00b4t still accessed but will probably visit soon, that is a corruption and mirror of the ultracompetitive and standarized school system in which they are immersed, with hateful students with no faces but codebars where the eyes should be. In my last Mage game, they had to do a trip to the Umbra, but was trying to save the Sanctum and it was memorable, but they liked to play in the city more)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T02:01:29-07:00","id":1311183,"title":"","content":"At last, my small bit of obscura is useful! <br /> <br /> There once a group of Rogue Primordials who didn't align with the Yozi/Neverborn who got jealous of the success of Creation. They didn't take the offer to help pitch in an make it when the OG crew were going around soliciting help. So they decided to make their own Creation and tried to bring it to Real Creation and it was shot down but the Godshrike (iirc) which either obliterated it or sent it back into the Deep Wyld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T05:44:11-07:00","id":1311198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1311183#post1311183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At last, my small bit of obscura is useful! <br /> <br /> There once a group of Rogue Primordials who didn't align with the Yozi/Neverborn who got jealous of the success of Creation. They didn't take the offer to help pitch in an make it when the OG crew were going around soliciting help. So they decided to make their own Creation and tried to bring it to Real Creation and it was shot down but the Godshrike (iirc) which either obliterated it or sent it back into the Deep Wyld.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you\u2019re thinking of Cemunian, the Constellation of Sinew and Dreams, and the world he crafted; it was the Unconquered Sun that reduced that world to cinders, not the Five-Metal Shrike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-10-2019, 08:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T05:54:58-07:00","id":1311200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1311183#post1311183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At last, my small bit of obscura is useful!<br /> <br /> There once a group of Rogue Primordials who didn't align with the Yozi/Neverborn who got jealous of the success of Creation. They didn't take the offer to help pitch in an make it when the OG crew were going around soliciting help. So they decided to make their own Creation and tried to bring it to Real Creation and it was shot down but the Godshrike (iirc) which either obliterated it or sent it back into the Deep Wyld.</div> </div> </div> </div>Slightly off, that one. The way the story goes, there was one jealous Primordial, Cemunian, Constellation of Sinew and Dream, who tried to displace and replace Creation with his own Creation, Cajerr\u00f3n. The Unconquered Sun used the Daystar's foremost weapon, the Apollyon Cannon, to send Cajerr\u00f3n back into the Wyld. (What Cemunian's issue was, we don't know; there were Primordials who weren't involved in the making of Creation, but it's not mentioned whether he was one of them.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T17:09:37-07:00","id":1311306,"title":"","content":"Neat. Thanks guys! I only remember reading about it on Tvtropes. I didn't start playing until 2nd Ed was wrapped up and I never went through all the books. I should probably download the older stuff and do a Lore Deep Dive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T17:12:09-07:00","id":1311308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1311306#post1311306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neat. Thanks guys! I only remember reading about it on Tvtropes. I didn't start playing until 2nd Ed was wrapped up and I never went through all the books. I should probably download the older stuff and do a Lore Deep Dive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah. I mean, there's <i>also </i>a lot of not-great stuff there. The Nameless Lair, the House of Succulent Tears, Lillun, et cetera.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T17:23:17-07:00","id":1311310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clophiroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1311167#post1311167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Although I have never been a fan of the Umbra. I like to focus my games in a region or city, and in the groups and characters living there and the consequences of their actions, and I find that when the players spend half the time exploring far-off realms to no real connections to the place they are playing in... It dilutes the style I like to play, and my players are also not fans of roaming, travelling characters. So... When I put pocket realms, they are localized things, with influence in the place they are playing in. In my current &quot;Occult investigators in a Japanese High School&quot; game there is a pocket realm, they haven\u00b4t still accessed but will probably visit soon, that is a corruption and mirror of the ultracompetitive and standarized school system in which they are immersed, with hateful students with no faces but codebars where the eyes should be. In my last Mage game, they had to do a trip to the Umbra, but was trying to save the Sanctum and it was memorable, but they liked to play in the city more)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not as familiar with the Umbra as with Chronicles of Darkness' Shadow, but wouldn't your scary version of the corresponding material world just be the local geography of the... let's call it animistic spirit world. The stuff that werewolves are spending most of their time stomping around in.<br /> <br /> I suppose that their spirit world wouldn't be precisely the same as the Shadow, but surely there's at least one layer in which one can realise metaphors without them all being self-contained pockets?<br /> <br /> I don't know, this is part of the problem of describing things just in terms of the Umbra to me, because it's the catch-all term for the entire World of Darkness cosmology outside of the material Earth. You've got the animistic spirit world, the land of the dead (or several), fairy/dream country, some kind of astral plane, pocket dimensions for things like vampire cities and private domains where mages can roam freely, the planets*, Cthulhu's house, and leprechauns.<br /> <br /> If a person is asking after how to get the Umbra into the setting of Exalted, are they talking about <i>all</i> of that?<br /> <br /> * It was supposed to be something like actual outer space was the Umbra as well, so it was the literal planets at the same time as they were supposed to turn out to be weird when you got to them, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T17:41:47-07:00","id":1311312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1311308#post1311308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah. I mean, there's <i>also </i>a lot of not-great stuff there. The Nameless Lair, the House of Succulent Tears, Lillun, et cetera.</div> </div> </div> </div>But on the other hand, there's good stuff too. <br /> <br /> I mean, after the first two chapters Infernals was good at least! And Alchemicals and CoCD: Autobot were rock solid, the CoCD was probably my favorite 2e book (which is why I keep hyping it here).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T19:55:57-07:00","id":1311329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1311312#post1311312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, after the first two chapters Infernals was good at least!</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s debatable. <br /> <br /> I will concede Autochthonian material, though it still doesn\u2019t beat Masters of Jade for my favorite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-10-2019, 11:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T20:10:45-07:00","id":1311330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1311310#post1311310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not as familiar with the Umbra as with Chronicles of Darkness' Shadow, but wouldn't your scary version of the corresponding material world just be the local geography of the... let's call it animistic spirit world. The stuff that werewolves are spending most of their time stomping around in.<br /> <br /> I suppose that their spirit world wouldn't be precisely the same as the Shadow, but surely there's at least one layer in which one can realise metaphors without them all being self-contained pockets?<br /> <br /> I don't know, this is part of the problem of describing things just in terms of the Umbra to me, because it's the catch-all term for the entire World of Darkness cosmology outside of the material Earth. You've got the animistic spirit world, the land of the dead (or several), fairy/dream country, some kind of astral plane, pocket dimensions for things like vampire cities and private domains where mages can roam freely, the planets*, Cthulhu's house, and leprechauns.<br /> <br /> If a person is asking after how to get the Umbra into the setting of Exalted, are they talking about <i>all</i> of that?<br /> <br /> * It was supposed to be something like actual outer space was the Umbra as well, so it was the literal planets at the same time as they were supposed to turn out to be weird when you got to them, right?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> In the game I\u00b4m playing in, there is no Umbra. There are some pocket zones. There is no outside the &quot;School&quot; you enter. No windows, no doors, impossible to leave except for the place you came from. THere is just... The place. The native inhabitants are just incapable of even thinking of the possibility of another place existing.<br /> <br /> Although yes, probably the distinction is pretty academical in game terms","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T21:20:33-07:00","id":1311333,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... keep it on topic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1311312#post1311312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, after the first two chapters Infernals was good at least!</div> </div> </div> </div>Or at least on forum topic...<br /> <br /> I feel that, on the whole, the first two chapters of Infernals aren't bad, they just have the wrong priorities. As the subject of this thread goes, regarding otherworldly landscapes and encounters, I'd say that some useful ideas can be gleaned from them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T21:50:23-07:00","id":1311335,"title":"","content":"The Yatani's Children claim to be from a place that isn't Creation (but clearly isn't any other dimension we know of), so there's possibly more than what we know (if you decide to accept them at their world for your own game's Creation).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T22:35:14-07:00","id":1311338,"title":"","content":"Previously there was also a kind of other Creation off in the Wyld called the Faraway I think, and also the reverse underside of creation where the Primordials stuck all their failed creations and experiments. Between those and all the other worlds mentioned there should be plenty out there beyond the wildest imaginings of creationites. There\u2019s also theoretically infinite potential and infinite possibilities in the Wyld. Of course if we lose the Lava Lamp Wyld you won\u2019t hear me complain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T23:57:04-07:00","id":1311351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1311306#post1311306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neat. Thanks guys! I only remember reading about it on Tvtropes. I didn't start playing until 2nd Ed was wrapped up and I never went through all the books. I should probably download the older stuff and do a Lore Deep Dive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although it's only a paragraph in the Daystar writeup, you want to track down the Ink Monkeys Ultimate Collection for Cemunian, and it should be a free download (although word of warning, it also contains 2e's Nameless Lair).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T02:40:59-07:00","id":1311367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1311338#post1311338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Previously there was also a kind of other Creation off in the Wyld called the Faraway I think, and also the reverse underside of creation where the Primordials stuck all their failed creations and experiments. Between those and all the other worlds mentioned there should be plenty out there beyond the wildest imaginings of creationites. There\u2019s also theoretically infinite potential and infinite possibilities in the Wyld. Of course if we lose the Lava Lamp Wyld you won\u2019t hear me complain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, in one of similar threads (which I was unaware of, when starting this one), Steven Lea Sheppard indirectly confirmed that Faraway exists in 3rd edition, since he's written that in 3e it's &quot;probably distinct from Zen-Mu.&quot; Thank you for pointing out Arms of the Chosen passage about Scorpion Empire. The relevant passage goes as follows (Arms of the Chosen, the last sentence on p 147):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some came from the chaos beyond reality\u2019s edge, others from dark and vasty depths under the world, and yet more from places that the Second Age has no name for or language to describe </div> </div> </div>So I think, it can be safely summarised that while focus has been turned to more &quot;low-keyish&quot; stuff, and probably not treated systematically in this edition, we can still expect a good number of stranger realms beyond Creation are still a thing.<br /> <br /> On a related note: some of people contributing to this thread have already mentioned some sources. As far as I understand, in Exalted there never was any equivalent of &quot;Beyond the Barriers: the book of worlds&quot; from WoD or &quot;Astral Realms&quot; from CoD. What books in Exalted did elaborate more on cosmology? I do not even mean a systematic treatment as much as a bunch of storyhooks. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T08:04:21-07:00","id":1311377,"title":"","content":"Though exactly what the Scorpion Empire is is a bit hazy. Masters of Jade implies that they're not Raksha, but the whole &quot;scorpion&quot; thing is reminiscent of Ishiika (Balor's weirdass scorpion sword). It might be a weird Freehold, though I'm leaning towards something else. 3e also has pockets of semi-stable Creation out in the Wyld, one is ruled by an Asura-like behemoth who used to hold up the sky way back when the Primoridals were making Creation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T08:07:05-07:00","id":1311380,"title":"","content":"There's also the Comet Gnosis, which may be one of Gaia'sThird Circle Devas but might be a pocket realm she made to traverse the Wyld more easily(it might be where Yatani's Children are from).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24948,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","user":"HamSandLich","date":". 05-11-2019, 11:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T08:24:03-07:00","id":1311384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1311377#post1311377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though exactly what the Scorpion Empire is is a bit hazy. Masters of Jade implies that they're not Raksha, but the whole &quot;scorpion&quot; thing is reminiscent of Ishiika (Balor's weirdass scorpion sword). It might be a weird Freehold, though I'm leaning towards something else. 3e also has pockets of semi-stable Creation out in the Wyld, one is ruled by an Asura-like behemoth who used to hold up the sky way back when the Primoridals were making Creation</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's been confirmed they're not Raksha in 3e, they're a different kind of Wyld creature. Apparently, they hurt to look at. Not much I can remember about dev answers on the topic past that though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T08:25:04-07:00","id":1311386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1311377#post1311377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. 3e also has pockets of semi-stable Creation out in the Wyld, one is ruled by an Asura-like behemoth who used to hold up the sky way back when the Primoridals were making Creation</div> </div> </div> </div>I missed that somewhere, that's pretty radical. Is that out of Lunars or did I miss it somewhere in other published books this edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T08:30:51-07:00","id":1311387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1311377#post1311377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Masters of Jade implies that they're not Raksha, but the whole &quot;scorpion&quot; thing is reminiscent of Ishiika (Balor's weirdass scorpion sword).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ishiika was merely tamed by Balor, and is an aspect of the shinma Nishkriya.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T08:42:28-07:00","id":1311389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1311386#post1311386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I missed that somewhere, that's pretty radical. Is that out of Lunars or did I miss it somewhere in other published books this edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Its in one of the &quot;Hundred Devils Night Parade&quot; publications, the one featuring the &quot;Strix&quot; and &quot;Zicnal the Asmani&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T08:45:22-07:00","id":1311390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1311387#post1311387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ishiika was merely tamed by Balor, and is an aspect of the shinma Nishkriya.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, though its appearance as a Scorpion specifically is used as a symbol by the Church of Balor(according to an old Vance post), and makes me wonder if the Scorpion Empire has some reverence for or connection to Nishkriya in its Ishiika aspect","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T08:55:38-07:00","id":1311391,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna regret this, but what are Nameless Lair and House of Tears?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T08:59:00-07:00","id":1311392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1311391#post1311391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna regret this, but what are Nameless Lair and House of Tears?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nameless Lair is Maha\u2019s hang out. In 2e it infamously had what I\u2019d describe as \u201crape pits\u201dz","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T09:03:48-07:00","id":1311394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1311391#post1311391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna regret this, but what are Nameless Lair and House of Tears?</div> </div> </div> </div>TW: RAPE<br /> <br /> Ok, now that that's out of the way, the Nameless Lair is the Elder Lunar Warlord Ma-Ha-Suchi's base of operations throughout the editions. In 1e-2e, he was a psychotic, wyld warped luddite with an irrational hatred of beauty and civilization. The Nameless Lair was a first age manse complex that contained an artificial Wyld Zone called the Rutting Pens, where he would keep captive men and women that he would systematically rape or have raped in order to produce wolf/goat beastmen offspring. He would then indoctrinate the beastmen into his insane social darwinist philosophy, using Wyld corruption to turn them into simplistic mental caricatures of themselves so they'd be an obedient barbarian horde with no nuance or capacity to rebel against his agenda.<br /> <br /> The House of Bitter Tears is a kingdom in the Labyrinth, near the lower levels of the maze and the Neverborn(this makes them actually more insane than most Deathlords), run by the vengeful spectres of a group of concubines that a FA solar raped to death. It provides ghost prostitutes to the beings of the Labyrinth to ravage as the will, with the twist being each of the ghost prostitutes is a former male serial rapist that's had their corpus multilated into a feminine shape and been enslaved to suffer the same treatment they inflicted upon women in life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24948,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","user":"HamSandLich","date":". 05-11-2019, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T09:22:01-07:00","id":1311400,"title":"","content":"Mind, these things are from past editions and well done-away with in 3e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T09:32:01-07:00","id":1311401,"title":"","content":"Well, the Nameless Lair and Ma-Ha-Suchi are still around, just toned down to something tolerable","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T09:37:11-07:00","id":1311402,"title":"","content":"Back to other realms of existence: FA solars also made a bunch of pocket dimensions stored in their artifacts. There's one in 3e inside of a soulsteel mace containing the soul of a dead sorcerer who you can bargain with for information. <br /> <br /> Oramus has his conceptual &quot;Beyond&quot; and arguably each of the Yozis is a pocket dimension in and of themselves. The Well of Udr was connected to both Oblivion and the conceptual space where worlds that never were crash against each other. When the Silver Chair and Daystar were still a thing, they were basically miniature worlds (moreso in the Silver Chair's case, being full of Luna's alter egos and places for her and Gaia to chill, the Daystar was just a huge fortress).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T09:43:08-07:00","id":1311403,"title":"","content":"DBs also has an Artifact where you can delve into another dimension in WFHW. The Ragara Artifact","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T09:48:43-07:00","id":1311404,"title":"","content":"Also, the Sea of Mind that the Forest Witches use, though whether that's an actual plane of existence or one big consensual hallucination is up for debate. The Forest of Oreythia itself is weird enough to to qualify as a pseudo wyld zone/shadowland(in that its a part of Creation where reality doesn't work as it should)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T11:23:15-07:00","id":1311410,"title":"","content":"For cosmology purposes and writeups of other realms, I would suggest looking into Games of Divinity from 1e and Compass of Celestial Directions: Wyld from 2e. Exalted: The Outcaste from 1e has the original writeup of the Forest Witches in it, which is probably the best example of just how weird Creation can get without having to tuck things into another realm.<br /> <br /> There are also other Celestial Compass books from 2e that look at the various other realms, so those are probably a place to look if you want more info about such places.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T12:02:32-07:00","id":1311418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1311410#post1311410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For cosmology purposes and writeups of other realms, I would suggest looking into Games of Divinity from 1e and Compass of Celestial Directions: Wyld from 2e. Exalted: The Outcaste from 1e has the original writeup of the Forest Witches in it, which is probably the best example of just how weird Creation can get without having to tuck things into another realm.<br /> <br /> There are also other Celestial Compass books from 2e that look at the various other realms, so those are probably a place to look if you want more info about such places.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anything of note is really added to Heaven or Hell in the Compass books that wasn't better written or more succinctly talked about in <b>Games of Divinity</b> or <b>Exalted: the Sidereals</b> myself. I think the 2e books kind of dwell on things that aren't really useful/intersting, or outright disruptive to their uses in games or as interesting places, so I would suggest the 1e books there.<br /> <br /> I think save Stygia in <b>Book of Bone &amp; Ebony</b>, nearly nothing in previous eiditon son the Underworld is going to fit really well with what it has been hinted at bieng so far in 3e. (Stygia is pretty easy to fit in as it's kind of central hub disconnected from any geography in Creation due to the new layout of the Underworld.)<br /> <br /> <b>CoCD: The Wyld </b>is not bad though. I can't really think to hate on it or not much, save it should be noted that probably anything it talks about the different Elemental Dragons at the Poles is also probably not holidng in 3e. But besides that, I think it gives good ideas of enviornments, wildlife, and all that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T12:19:48-07:00","id":1311420,"title":"","content":"The Labyrinth will probably be unchanged(except for maybe the House of Bitter Tears), and some of the more unique Underworld kingdoms, like the one with two queens who swap places with the seasons, as neither of those particularly map to anything in Creation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T12:21:49-07:00","id":1311421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1311367#post1311367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, in one of similar threads (which I was unaware of, when starting this one), Steven Lea Sheppard indirectly confirmed that Faraway exists in 3rd edition, since he's written that in 3e it's &quot;probably distinct from Zen-Mu.&quot; Thank you for pointing out Arms of the Chosen passage about Scorpion Empire. The relevant passage goes as follows (Arms of the Chosen, the last sentence on p 147):<br /> <br /> So I think, it can be safely summarised that while focus has been turned to more &quot;low-keyish&quot; stuff, and probably not treated systematically in this edition, we can still expect a good number of stranger realms beyond Creation are still a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>A big way to think on this is that Exalted, while having other realms of existance, still very much wants games focused on Creation. I think a theme you notice is that the stuff beyond Creation aren't so much like Umbral realms but entire other stable worlds in the Wyld...and which due to being kind &quot;convergently evolved&quot; to things that might or might not make sense to folks in Creaiton. You're not likely going ot see soemthing like the Werewolf Deep Umbra, and instead more likely things that are just outright <i>alein</i> or strange. This is a bit due to the genres of fantasy Exalted draws on, wherein there's less an astral plane and more that there's &quot;Weird shit beyond the chaos&quot;, as shown in stories like the Black Company, the Flat Earth, or parts of the Lovecraft mythos.<br /> <br /> I think a big thing too is that while we'll see more, save for areas important to understanidng major chunks of the setting (Heaven, Hell, the Underworld, the Wyld), a lot of these places like Zen-Mu, the Farway, and the Scorpion Empire are going to likely not ever receive more than vague hints and tidbits. Or they are accessable story elements useful for a partiuclar plot htread, like the pseudo-reality of the Sea of MInd that the Forest Witches go into, or the entire city found wihtin the shield in the Dragon-Blooded book. These aren't htings that are part of some bigger cosmic statement of the setting, but specific elements that their bizarre points of entry and the worlds in them are interesting because of how they relate to Creation, or how strange it is that they are there in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1311367#post1311367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a related note: some of people contributing to this thread have already mentioned some sources. As far as I understand, in Exalted there never was any equivalent of &quot;Beyond the Barriers: the book of worlds&quot; from WoD or &quot;Astral Realms&quot; from CoD. What books in Exalted did elaborate more on cosmology? I do not even mean a systematic treatment as much as a bunch of storyhooks.</div> </div> </div> </div>My shortlist of things to check on:<ul><li><b>Exalted Third Editon </b>- Describes more or less the main stuff, like the structure of Creation, its relation ot the Wyld, Heaven, Hell, and the Underworld, and how they relate together. Not in super depth but I think enough to give pretty good base knowledge, especially how the different realms of existance to some extent have a much more &quot;physical&quot; connection in a way that they don't in WoD.</li> <li><b>Games of Divinity</b> - Talks about Yu-Shan (Heaven) and Malfeas (Hell) to pretty good extent and gives a good idea of how they relate with Creation. It's an older book but does this discussion in a pretty succinct way that doesn't get too bogged down with the need to keep adding to something htere later entries did.</li> <li><b>Exalted: the Sidereals</b> - The 1e book on Sidereals I feel does a pretty good job of exploring Heaven in the second chapter, especially in a way that's pretty succinct and gives good ideas of how it operates. It I think highlights a bit like Malfeas in the previous book how the different realms of existance in Creation are more places extending the setting rather than separate other worlds, at least for major ones worth dicussing in broader contexts.</li> <li><b>The Book of Bone &amp; Ebony</b> - The first chapter of this book about Sygia is actually the best stuff in the gameline about anything in the Underworld. Not a lot in 3e is actually using the other bits of this or other depictions though, and I don't think even a lot beyond that chapter is likely to hold either, but I think it's still a pretty good cahpter.</li> <li><b>Compass of Celestial DIrection: The Wyld</b> is a pretty solid discussion of the world beyond Creation, and the things that inhabit it. It's kind of out of date again since some of the bits in it will not hold in 3e and didn't hold before it, such as the names fo the Elemetnal Dragons, the existance of Pure Chaos or the socities of the Fair Folk quite. But htere's some good ideas of what the world does when it &quot;breaks down&quot; so to speak.</li> <li><b>Compass of Celestial Direction: Autochthona </b>has been mentioend and I suggest it too. The body of Autochthon and all that is a pretty exotic, and strange place. What I like about it again compared to a WoD world is that it's still a place where you have countries, cities, and civilizations doing their things in there. It's also probably the best written of the different &quot;Compass&quot; books in 2e by far, and I think a good idea of how to think of other areas of the setting.</li> <li><b>Ink Monkeys, &quot;Chapter Seven: The Fair Folk&quot;</b> - I think this is actaully probably the better way to kind of conceive the way in which the residents of the Wyld interact with Creation than anything really in the hardcovers. WHile there is some nice prose in the 1e Fair Folk book, I think that they as a whole don't give a lot of good information on cosmology of the setting, or at least, cosmology that doesn't just lead to stuff not pertinant to games or discussions like angels on pinehads. (This is from someone who quite likes things like the shinma, but ultimatley thinks they didn't do well for the setting.)</li> </ul><br /> I think these are going to give you some of the most thurough stuff if your interests are with the relams beyond Creation. And namely, stuff that I think is going ot hold in 3e and was more o rless consistent all three editons. A lot fhte details beyond what I note are likely no longer holding, or very particular ot a specific edition, and so will end up having to be considered in the way different settings relate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T12:22:57-07:00","id":1311422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1311420#post1311420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Labyrinth will probably be unchanged(except for maybe the House of Bitter Tears), and some of the more unique Underworld kingdoms, like the one with two queens who swap places with the seasons, as neither of those particularly map to anything in Creation</div> </div> </div> </div>The Labyrinth likely is still there yeah, but I wouldn't be surprised if some of the details isn't. I kind of doubt it'll have the nice ordelry reference-to-Dante bolgia about for instance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T12:45:18-07:00","id":1311424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1311420#post1311420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Labyrinth will probably be unchanged(except for maybe the House of Bitter Tears), and some of the more unique Underworld kingdoms, like the one with two queens who swap places with the seasons, as neither of those particularly map to anything in Creation</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt it'll be unchanged, as much as it'll still be called the Labyrinth and in general will serve a similar purpose but with MUCH better writing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T12:52:25-07:00","id":1311427,"title":"","content":"Oh, for sure, but in terms of being an eldritch cthonic realm inhabited by transhuman and never-were-human ghosts that laughs at the normal constraints of space-time and has a tendency to drive things insane, it'll be the same as previous editions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T16:23:41-07:00","id":1311448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1311390#post1311390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, though its appearance as a Scorpion specifically is used as a symbol by the Church of Balor(according to an old Vance post), and makes me wonder if the Scorpion Empire has some reverence for or connection to Nishkriya in its Ishiika aspect</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh the scorpion as the emblem of the Church of Balor goes all the way back to First Edition. I'd say it's a matter of the grass-cutter scythe being an iconic symbol for him, even if it remains a separate entity from him that is conceivably independent with his absence.<br /> <br /> I had a notion of the Empire being distantly connected to Ishiika by way of mythology using a few other Nishkriya aspects shortly after Masters of Jade came out, but that was something taking the name a bit literally. It did invoke the imagery of mating dances and riding on the backs of parents, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1311402#post1311402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oramus has his conceptual &quot;Beyond&quot; and arguably each of the Yozis is a pocket dimension in and of themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though all of the Yozis being worlds was something that became a bit over-emphasized at one point, and kind of detracts from the original presentation of Adorjan, the Ebon Dragon and She Who Lives in Her Name.<br /> <br /> If I'm being honest, for a while I've not been particularly happy with the idea that the true form of Isidoros is a coded black hole. It feels to me like it's making the Yozis more uniform and less mythic.<br /> <br /> And the Beyond of Oramus is a far too overwrought concept. It's adding this whole other layer to the cosmology that alternately just rips off pre-existing parts and does nothing at all, while also really talking itself up. I think it's unnecessary to make Oramus a kind of uber-Primordial when they're all being given back a bit of mystery and grandeur.<br /> <br /> For the Labyrinth, my tastes and my biases would have me hope that it's something that goes a bit subtler and deeper. Less in-your-face horror, more the bleak, creeping dread of inevitable mortality.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T16:50:12-07:00","id":1311453,"title":"","content":"I always imagined the Labyrinth as shout-out to ancient cthonic practices that saw caves as an entrance to the underworld. Those who traverse it can gain great power and a twisted form of enlightenment, but only by partaking of the abyss and resolving it's themes with themselves(whether that's turning into a gibbering lunatic or getting really zen should be up to the individual). If anyone has read <i>The Second Apocalypse</i> series by R.S. Bakker, the Holy Deep of the Nonmen is pretty close to what i'm thinking of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T16:55:24-07:00","id":1311455,"title":"","content":"Hmmm.... I will grant that it was wrong of me to say that all Yozis have their own internal worlds. Adorjan especially doesn\u2019t seem like she would bother to be bigger than she currently cares to be or to keep part of herself separate from others. That said, I also think Isidoros is capable of being a black hole, a giant boar, and plenty of other things besides and I don\u2019t think comparing Yozis to the largest, most magnificent real-world universal phenomena we can perceive is necessarily wrong, even if it might be incomplete.<br /> <br /> As for the Beyond.... hmmmm..... Honestly, the main distinction between it and the Wyld in my mind is that you can visit the Wyld without suffering sudden existence failure, while the Beyond should be sufficiently alien to preclude that. Which.... yeah, doesn\u2019t really feel like enough of a hook for it to actually matter much, except as another \u201cWeird Oramus Thing\u201d and there are probably better ways to write about his weirdness. That said, there\u2019s a part of me that still likes the concept of the Beyond, and wants to use the first (and only) First Age expedition into it as a justification for some freaky stuff, but I think that\u2019s mainly because.... the Wyld has become this \u201cknown\u201d thing and having a thing that can literally be defined to be unknowable, even by First Age savants, is cool.<br /> <br /> Which is honestly probably more of a commentary on how the Wyld has been handled. For the endless Chaos outside reality to become boring, that feels like it\u2019s a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T18:36:08-07:00","id":1311471,"title":"","content":"I'd love to see pocket worlds built by ancient solars introduced","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T20:00:41-07:00","id":1311482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1311453#post1311453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always imagined the Labyrinth as shout-out to ancient cthonic practices that saw caves as an entrance to the underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your point of that reminds me of The Tombs of Atuan from Ursula LeGuin's Earthsea; a setting and story in which the horror comes from the isolation, the sensory deprivation and the being hopelessly lost and trapped. A place steeped in death in the sense of having ancient treasures entombed beyond hope of acquisition deep within them and in which people might be abandoned to slowly dehydrate, which its worshippers regard as the place devouring them.<br /> <br /> Hmm, that also reminds me of the subtle dread inherent to the Paths of the Dead as they appear in their original story; I don't quite object to Peter Jackson's decision to <i><span style=\"color:#0000ff\">electrify </span></i>them for the sake of the visual medium and more fast-paced story, but I know which I would prefer informing the depths of the Underworld.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those who traverse it can gain great power and a twisted form of enlightenment, but only by partaking of the abyss and resolving it's themes with themselves(whether that's turning into a gibbering lunatic or getting really zen should be up to the individual).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I find the idea that ghosts, some necromancers and the odd other adventurer descend into the Labyrinth and emerge changed to be compelling. I just prefer the idea that what they found down there was more low-key in its soul-chilling horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-12T09:55:32-07:00","id":1311577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1311471#post1311471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love to see pocket worlds built by ancient solars introduced</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s worth noting that the 3e Quickstart Adventure, Tomb of Dreams, takes place inside a powerful demon that some ancient solars turned inside out and made into a pocket world in order to seal away some artifacts. So, that\u2019s a thing you can do too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-12T15:38:54-07:00","id":1311622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1311577#post1311577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s worth noting that the 3e Quickstart Adventure, Tomb of Dreams, takes place inside a powerful demon that some ancient solars turned inside out and made into a pocket world in order to seal away some artifacts. So, that\u2019s a thing you can do too.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What the fuck is with Solars and turning demons inside out to hold things? First Malfeas, now this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-12T18:02:32-07:00","id":1311663,"title":"","content":"One might get the idea that the Solars of the First Age had some form of bizarre eversion fetish","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-12T21:09:16-07:00","id":1311701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1311622#post1311622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What the fuck is with Solars and turning demons inside out to hold things? First Malfeas, now this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, you ever try to make a Klein bottle in three dimensions from non-demons?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T16:19:37-07:00","id":1320354,"title":"","content":"After reading a question in &quot;Ask the Devs&quot; thread, I read what 1e Abyssals says about the Well of Udr.<br /> <br /> Well, it explicitly says that it leads to Labirynth, actually twice.<br /> <br /> It says that Dowager &quot;learned about other Universes&quot; and that she thinks that the Well leads somewhere and plans to escape there. The book says that in that hope, she's wrong.<br /> <br /> I have two questions: <br /> <br /> 1. I read here and there on forums and wikies that the Well is a crossroads between worlds. Nothing in 1e Abyssals indicates that, quite to the contrary. Is there any evidence that this used to be a canon version? Actually, I hope so, because that option is immensly cool.<br /> <br /> 2. Does &quot;learn&quot; above indicates that Dowager is factually right about the existence of other universes? Is there any other bit of Exalted canon in any edition which suggests so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 06-23-2019, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T17:10:38-07:00","id":1320361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1320354#post1320354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After reading a question in &quot;Ask the Devs&quot; thread, I read what 1e Abyssals says about the Well of Udr.<br /> <br /> Well, it explicitly says that it leads to Labirynth, actually twice.<br /> <br /> It says that Dowager &quot;learned about other Universes&quot; and that she thinks that the Well leads somewhere and plans to escape there. The book says that in that hope, she's wrong.<br /> <br /> I have two questions:<br /> <br /> 1. I read here and there on forums and wikies that the Well is a crossroads between worlds. Nothing in 1e Abyssals indicates that, quite to the contrary. Is there any evidence that this used to be a canon version? Actually, I hope so, because that option is immensly cool.<br /> <br /> 2. Does &quot;learn&quot; above indicates that Dowager is factually right about the existence of other universes? Is there any other bit of Exalted canon in any edition which suggests so?</div> </div> </div> </div>The 1e take is pretty much all there was on it in 1e. It didn't become a gateway for-sure to toher worlds until Second Edition, which is only canon within itself. And whether or not what's in there is what she thinks is in there is never given a definitive answer, just what she thinks it is I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T19:12:34-07:00","id":1320375,"title":"","content":"I like the idea Dreams exist as a plane of existence that can be reached. And its tied to worlds of memory and hidden Yozis/Primordial.<br /> <br /> And several 3rd Circle Souls I imagine are worlds or planes of Existence. I had a soul of the Ebon Dragon known as the White Zone that existed as a two dimensional plane others could travel to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T00:13:18-07:00","id":1320423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1320354#post1320354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After reading a question in &quot;Ask the Devs&quot; thread, I read what 1e Abyssals says about the Well of Udr.<br /> <br /> Well, it explicitly says that it leads to Labirynth, actually twice.<br /> <br /> It says that Dowager &quot;learned about other Universes&quot; and that she thinks that the Well leads somewhere and plans to escape there. The book says that in that hope, she's wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>So yeah, I was the one who asked the original question, because I found what 1e Abyssals said was contradictory, given Dowager was the one who'd studied the Well the most. If it led to the Labyrinth alone, then she'd know that, ergo she has reason to think it leads, or can lead, elsewhere.<br /> <br /> So there was either an unspoken assumption in 1e that the Well can lead to more than one place, or there were two different ideas of where it can lead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T01:16:36-07:00","id":1320428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1320423#post1320423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So yeah, I was the one who asked the original question, because I found what 1e Abyssals said was contradictory, given Dowager was the one who'd studied the Well the most. If it led to the Labyrinth alone, then she'd know that, ergo she has reason to think it leads, or can lead, elsewhere.<br /> <br /> So there was either an unspoken assumption in 1e that the Well can lead to more than one place, or there were two different ideas of where it can lead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or that the Dowager is crazy as hell. That's also an option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T02:34:26-07:00","id":1320437,"title":"","content":"Actually, to me 1e text says almost explicitly that:<br /> - Well of Udr leads to Labirynth (this is completely explicit);<br /> - There are other universes (Dowager &quot;learned&quot; this; the choice of the word seems to strongly imply that she was actually right about it);<br /> - The Well doesn't lead to the these universes (the text says that Dowager is wrong about possibility of escape, but this is vague. Maybe she just won't make it before it's too late or will be chased afterwards).<br /> <br /> But yes, is appears that there were two different ideas of what Well of Udr should be and writers were not consistent about it (apparent contradictions are separated in the book).<br /> <br /> Why I asked this question is that many people, including Stephen Lea Sheppard, claimed on forums that 2e retconned Well of Udr to lead to Oblivion while in 1e there was more to it. So I was wondering where this idea that Well of Udr leads to every world comes from and I assumed it should be some other source in 1e. Is it maybe detailed in the Book of Bone and Ebony?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 06-24-2019, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T03:25:13-07:00","id":1320443,"title":"","content":"The discussion this is taking off with is why I kind of hate the Well of Udr.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T03:59:00-07:00","id":1320449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1320423#post1320423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it led to the Labyrinth alone, then she'd know that\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Would</i> she?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:white\">The Labyrinth isn\u2019t exactly known for being absolutely uniform in appearance across its entirety.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T04:58:03-07:00","id":1320459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1320443#post1320443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The discussion this is taking off with is why I kind of hate the Well of Udr.</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of curiosity: why? (Seriously, it's not meant to be provocative.)<br /> <br /> For me, it's an example of good world-building for a game like this: some very evocative way for leaving potentially infinite possibilities while not over-explaining things.<br /> <br /> Personally, I have a sweet-spot for the trope of &quot;there's even more to this&quot;, where frames of the world sketched so far actually turn out to be part of even stranger and greater cosmology.<br /> <br /> Of course, sometimes it doesn't fit or is plainly goofy. It wouldn't fit Middle Earth. But for Exalted this dash of silver-age comic book weirdness seems more than appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T11:56:44-07:00","id":1320541,"title":"","content":"I kinda like it being one of the few things related to the Abyss that isn't wholly destructive. I mean, sure the Dowager used it for destruction, but its not bound by that limitation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T03:55:27-07:00","id":1320709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1310979-other-planes-of-existence?p=1320459#post1320459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Out of curiosity: why? </div> </div> </div> </div>I had a thing prepared to say critical of alternate realities, but... they apparently didn't apply when I read about the Dragon Blooded group Yatani's Children.<br /> <br /> I kind of want to at least retain a measure of it for something from the Underworld, but... Why? I have some notions of my own that would place the Well as an example of something cosmologically weird and a kind of proto-Underworld from the earliest days of Creation. The backstory given for the Underworld kind of fits with the possibility that it might intersect with reality in strange ways.<br /> <br /> Disregard my prior statement, much of my viewpoint is being revised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}